### FENIX with the sim-on-fhir FHIR package (config/sim-on-fhir-package.yaml)
#
# Profiles, ValueSets and ObservationDefinitions come from ../sim-on-fhir/output/package.tgz,
# SNOMED/LOINC from the Nationale Terminologieserver (NTS_USERNAME / NTS_PASSWORD in config/.env).
# Data: the "sim" test data (test/data/sim/), queries in queries/sim/fhir/.
#
# Setup (once, and again after a new IG build or changed test data):
#   go run ./cmd/fenix -config config/sim-on-fhir-package.yaml -cmd load sim
# Start the API server:
#   go run ./cmd/fenix -config config/sim-on-fhir-package.yaml -cmd serve -source sim
#
# Test data for the sb-ibd dataset (adults; the older rows 123/456/789/... are children):
#   2001  DBC S2001: zorgtype 11, 0313|922, open since 2020-03-01      -> in the Group
#         Verrichting V1 038853 (2021, in the IBD list), V3 190008 (not in the list)
#         Calprotectin 101 (2021, local code FCAL, not mapped), 103 (2017, LOINC)
#                                                Vragenlijst Q1 (2024)
#   2002  DBC S2002: zorgtype 21, 0318|601, 2019-06-01..2021-06-01      -> in the Group
#         Verrichting V2 035121 (2020), V4 038853 (2017)
#         Calprotectin 102 (2020), 108 (2022, no result), both local code FCAL, not mapped
#                                                Vragenlijst Q2 (2017)
#   2003  DBC S2003: other diagnosis 0313|100                           -> not in the Group
#   2004  DBC S2004: 0313|922 but 2015..2016 (before 2018)              -> not in the Group
#   2005  DBC S2005: 0313|923 but DBCgeldig=false (entered-in-error)    -> not in the Group
#
# The calprotectin of 2001 and 2002 is delivered under the local lab code FCAL, which no concept map
# translates, so the $export below holds no Observation with LOINC 38445-3: the findings get
# FX-DATA-042 "code filtered on (code) occurs in no exported resource" at Observation.code.coding.code
# for k363-calprotectin-before-scopie. The dashboard offers to map a source code to 38445-3; mapping
# FCAL -> 38445-3 brings 101, 102 and 108 back, and 108 (no result) then gives FX-DATA-040 for value[x].

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@base = {{host}}/r4

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Observation queries (as in group-demo.http)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Every Observation
GET {{base}}/Observation
Accept: application/fhir+json

### All Observations of patient 123
GET {{base}}/Observation?patient=123
Accept: application/fhir+json

### One code (pushed down into SQL)
GET {{base}}/Observation?code=MCD_A
Accept: application/fhir+json

### OR list in a pushed-down param — MCD_A and MCD_B
GET {{base}}/Observation?code=MCD_A,MCD_B
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Calprotectin since 2018 — none: 101, 102, 108 carry the unmapped local code FCAL, 103 is from 2017
GET {{base}}/Observation?code=http://loinc.org|38445-3&date=ge2018-01-01
Accept: application/fhir+json

### code:in the ObservationCodesSan ValueSet from the package — 103 (101, 102, 108 are FCAL, not mapped)
GET {{base}}/Observation?code:in=https://ig.santeon.nl/sim-on-fhir/ValueSet/observation-codes-san
Accept: application/fhir+json

### code:in an unknown ValueSet — refused with an OperationOutcome instead of silently returning everything
GET {{base}}/Observation?code:in=https://example.org/ValueSet/unknown
Accept: application/fhir+json

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### The sb-ibd member-filter and export searches, one by one
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Adults — 2001..2005
GET {{base}}/Patient?birthdate=le2008-11-20
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Every DBC as EpisodeOfCare — S2001..S2005
GET {{base}}/EpisodeOfCare
Accept: application/fhir+json

### status (S2005 is entered-in-error) — S2001..S2004
GET {{base}}/EpisodeOfCare?status=active,finished
Accept: application/fhir+json

### date on the period (S2004 ended in 2016) — S2001, S2002, S2003, S2005
GET {{base}}/EpisodeOfCare?date=ge2018-01-01
Accept: application/fhir+json

### The DBC diagnosis as Condition
GET {{base}}/Condition?code=urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|922,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|601
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Chained: the EpisodeOfCare whose Condition has an IBD diagnosis — S2001, S2002, S2004, S2005
GET {{base}}/EpisodeOfCare?condition:Condition.code=urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|922,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|923,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|601,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|602
Accept: application/fhir+json

### The whole EpisodeOfCare member-filter — S2001 and S2002
GET {{base}}/EpisodeOfCare?type=https://declaratie.nza.nl/zorgtype|11,https://declaratie.nza.nl/zorgtype|21&status=active,finished&date=ge2018-01-01&condition:Condition.code=urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|922,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|923,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|601,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|602
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Procedures in the IBD list since 2018 — V1 and V2 (V3 not in the list, V4 from 2017)
GET {{base}}/Procedure?code:in=https://ig.santeon.nl/sim-on-fhir/ValueSet/ibd-verrichting-codes-nza&date=ge2018-01-01
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Questionnaire since 2018 — Q1 (Q2 is from 2017)
GET {{base}}/QuestionnaireResponse?questionnaire=http://decor.nictiz.nl/fhir/Questionnaire/2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.11.60.124.27.62--20250714064425&authored=ge2018-01-01
Accept: application/fhir+json

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Conformance resources from the package (and its dependencies)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Loaded packages: one ImplementationGuide per package
GET {{base}}/ImplementationGuide?_count=20
Accept: application/fhir+json

### A profile by canonical url
GET {{base}}/StructureDefinition?url=https://ig.santeon.nl/sim-on-fhir/StructureDefinition/observation-san
Accept: application/fhir+json

### The ObservationDefinitions
GET {{base}}/ObservationDefinition
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Expand a ValueSet from the package (expansion-source "local")
GET {{base}}/ValueSet/$expand?url=https://ig.santeon.nl/sim-on-fhir/ValueSet/ibd-verrichting-codes-nza&count=10
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Expand a SNOMED ECL set on the NTS (expansion-source "nts"; needs the NTS credentials)
GET {{base}}/ValueSet/$expand?url=http://snomed.info/sct?fhir_vs=ecl/%3C%3C%2077176002%20OR%20%3C%3C%208392000%20OR%20%3C%3C%208517006
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Validate a code against a ValueSet
GET {{base}}/ValueSet/$validate-code?url=https://ig.santeon.nl/sim-on-fhir/ValueSet/observation-codes-san&system=http://loinc.org&code=38445-3
Accept: application/fhir+json

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### The generated sb-ibd Group and export, exactly as generated by sim-on-fhir
### (fsh-generated/resources/Group-sb-ibd-cohort.json and Parameters-sb-ibd-export.json).
### FENIX reads the Bulk Data member-filters (modifierExtension + valueExpression) and fills
### {today-18y} in on every run.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# @name sbIbdGroup
POST {{base}}/Group
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Group",
  "id": "sb-ibd-cohort",
  "type": "person",
  "actual": true,
  "name": "sb-ibd Group",
  "modifierExtension": [
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/bulkdata/StructureDefinition/member-filter",
      "valueExpression": {
        "language": "application/x-fhir-query",
        "expression": "Patient?birthdate=le{today-18y}"
      }
    },
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/bulkdata/StructureDefinition/member-filter",
      "valueExpression": {
        "language": "application/x-fhir-query",
        "expression": "EpisodeOfCare?type=https://declaratie.nza.nl/zorgtype|11,https://declaratie.nza.nl/zorgtype|21&status=active,finished&date=ge2018-01-01&condition:Condition.code=urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|922,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.313|923,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|601,urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.27.15.4.318|602"
      }
    }
  ]
}

### Resolve its members — quantity 2 (patients 2001 and 2002)
GET {{base}}/Group/{{sbIbdGroup.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### $export with the generated sb-ibd parameters (FENIX takes them as query parameters,
### not as a Parameters body). Result: no Observation (FCAL is not mapped, see the top) / Patient 2001, 2002 /
### Procedure V1, V2 / QuestionnaireResponse Q1.
# @name sbIbdExport
POST {{base}}/Group/{{sbIbdGroup.response.body.id}}/$export?_type=Procedure%2CObservation%2CQuestionnaireResponse%2CPatient&_typeFilter=Procedure%3Fcode%3Ain%3Dhttps%3A%2F%2Fig.santeon.nl%2Fsim-on-fhir%2FValueSet%2Fibd-verrichting-codes-nza%26date%3Dge2018-01-01&_typeFilter=Observation%3Fcode%3Dhttp%3A%2F%2Floinc.org%7C38445-3%26date%3Dge2018-01-01&_typeFilter=QuestionnaireResponse%3Fquestionnaire%3Dhttp%3A%2F%2Fdecor.nictiz.nl%2Ffhir%2FQuestionnaire%2F2.16.840.1.113883.2.4.3.11.60.124.27.62--20250714064425%26authored%3Dge2018-01-01&_typeFilter=Patient%3Fgender%3Dmale%2Cfemale&_elements=Procedure.identifier%2CProcedure.code%2CProcedure.performed%5Bx%5D%2CProcedure.subject%2CObservation.identifier%2CObservation.code%2CObservation.value%5Bx%5D%2CObservation.effective%5Bx%5D%2CObservation.subject%2CQuestionnaireResponse.identifier%2CQuestionnaireResponse.questionnaire%2CQuestionnaireResponse.authored%2CQuestionnaireResponse.item%2CQuestionnaireResponse.subject%2CPatient.identifier%2CPatient.gender%2CPatient.birthDate
Accept: application/fhir+json
Prefer: respond-async

### Export status (the Content-Location of the kick-off): one NDJSON file per type
GET {{host}}{{sbIbdExport.response.headers.Content-Location}}
Accept: application/json
